# frontend/.dockerignore
# KindPDF — files to exclude from the Docker build context
#
# WHY node_modules IS CRITICAL TO EXCLUDE:
#   The Dockerfile runs "npm ci" inside the container, which installs clean,
#   Linux-native dependencies — including platform-specific binaries for tools
#   like esbuild (used by Tailwind v3 internally via jiti).
#
#   Without this file, "COPY . ." sends the host's node_modules (built on
#   Windows) into the Docker build context and overwrites the Linux-native
#   modules that npm ci just installed. The Windows esbuild binary does not
#   run on Linux, so Tailwind cannot scan source files for classes, and the
#   compiled CSS file contains only ~26KB of browser resets with zero utility
#   classes. Result: the app renders as completely unstyled HTML.
#
#   Excluding node_modules here means "COPY . ." only copies source code.
#   The container uses its own Linux-native node_modules from npm ci instead.
#
# SIDE BENEFIT: Excluding node_modules also makes builds much faster —
#   node_modules is typically 200–400MB and slow to send to the Docker daemon.

node_modules
build
.env
.env.*
npm-debug.log*
